      {
        "id": "p63-question-22-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{e^x}{e^x+1}\\,dx$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\ln(e^x+1)+C$",
          "worked": "The denominator is $f(x)=e^x+1$, with $f'(x)=e^x$. Since $e^x+1>0$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\frac{e^x}{e^x+1}\\,dx&=\\ln|e^x+1|+C\\\\&=\\ln(e^x+1)+C.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p63-question-22-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find $\\displaystyle\\int_1^e\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x^2}\\right)^2\\,dx$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{e^3-e^{-3}}{3}+2$",
          "worked": "Expanding:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x^2}\\right)^2&=x^2+\\frac{2}{x}+x^{-4}.\n\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int_1^e\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x^2}\\right)^2\\,dx&=\\int_1^e\\left(x^2+\\frac{2}{x}+x^{-4}\\right)\\,dx\\\\&=\\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}+2\\ln x-\\frac{x^{-3}}{3}\\right]_1^e\\\\&=\\left(\\frac{e^3}{3}+2-\\frac{1}{3e^3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac13+0-\\frac13\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{e^3}{3}+2-\\frac{1}{3e^3}-0\\\\&=\\frac{e^3-e^{-3}}{3}+2.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
